From 487c87f6755a96651ec4e906653e92561110369c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:45:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(pi-compat): do not charge a tool guard for the time
 the user takes to answer

A permission-style tool_call guard that asked the user was denied after the
10 s handler budget while its dialog was still open, so slow approvals were
refused. Time spent awaiting ctx.ui dialogs is now excluded, capped below the
host's 30 s request timeout so a guard whose dialog never settles still fails
closed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
